  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Run a BFF primordial-soup simulation of random 64-byte programs epoch by epoch and examine it: population grid and diversity/entropy/complexity metrics, per-organism genome, lineage and instruction distribution, a hand-stepped interpreter debugger for a pair of tapes, replicator scans, checkpoint/resume through a run browser, and metric overlays across stored runs. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
